<h1>Employment Leave Act Readiness</h1>
<p>The outcome of future legislative change may require significant payroll system, policy and process updates 
across many organisations.</p>
<p>Businesses that leave preparation until the last minute may face unnecessary risk, disruption and cost.</p>
<h2>Readiness Assessment</h2>
<ul>
<li>Payroll process reviews</li>
<li>Payroll platform configuration reviews</li>
<li>Employment agreement considerations</li>
<li>Leave management processes</li>
<li>Compliance gap analysis</li>
</ul>
<h2>Payroll and Technology Impacts</h2>
<p>Legislative change frequently drives payroll system changes. Preparation involves understanding how payroll practices, 
configuration settings and business processes may need to evolve.</p>
<h2>Transition Planning</h2>
<p>True Blue Payroll helps businesses understand how proposed changes may affect payroll operations and what 
preparation activities can be undertaken to reduce implementation risk.</p>
<h2>Independent Perspective</h2>
<p>The focus is on practical payroll realities, helping businesses understand which aspects of their 
payroll environment may require review, redesign or remediation.</p>
</main>
